n":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.6357,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Verified in scratch: fails on anyio 4.14.2' is attached only to the first bullet.","AC: 'for both a successful and a raising drive'."],"finding":"The scratch verification covers only the successful-drive test. The raising-drive (403-shape) variant is listed as 'must also leave the loop collectable', yet the AC requires it to fail on 4.14.2, and the plan never says it was or will be checked RED.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f772f27ab60a96cd3","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing: 'Failure path: the same test with the drive raising inside the coroutine'","norm_id":"n743d0e105a2329b9","priority":0.3143,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The raising variant catches the exception inside the coroutine, which drops the traceback→frame→client edge from the referrer chain, so the test passes on 4.14.2 too."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5714,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the measurement harness (path or inline command: 12 `verify_completion` runs on daemon threads, dummy Bedrock creds) and a numeric 'flat' bound (e.g. per-run block delta < 1% of the 4.14.2 delta and service-model OrderedDict count not growing per run).","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["F1","E6","E2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.3486,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'the scratch measurement shows flat allocated blocks' — no command and no bound.","Root cause: 'anyio 4.15.0 -> flat (543,052 -> 544,109 blocks over 4 runs, 7 OrderedDicts)'."],"finding":"The ≥10-run measurement AC has no reproducible harness or command, and 'flat' has no threshold. The plan does not say whether the scratch script is committed or how it is invoked, and the only 4.15.0 data so far covers 4 runs, not ≥10.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f95efd03be174ce4e","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria: 'Per-run growth is removed, measured over at least 10 gate runs in one process ... flat allocated blocks'","norm_id":"nb93575d23b200915","priority":0.2514,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The executor runs a different harness (no daemon threads, or no 403 path) and reports 'flat'.","Small residual growth (~260 blocks/run) is judged flat by one person and leaky by another."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Define flat as: over 12 runs, total block growth < 5,000 and the service-model OrderedDict count does not grow with run count. Record the before (4.14.2) and after (locked) numbers from the same harness in the ticket comment.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5714,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Align the title with the measured metric: '~115k allocated blocks (~18.4k service-model OrderedDicts)'.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["E1","COH"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.6,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Title: 'leaves about 100k Python objects (botocore service-model data) alive'","Context: 'leaves about 115k allocated blocks alive (18,437 botocore service-model `OrderedDict`s per run)'"],"finding":"The title and body disagree on magnitude and unit. The title says 'about 100k Python objects'; the body measures 'about 115k allocated blocks' and 18,437 OrderedDicts. Allocated blocks (tracemalloc) are not Python objects.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5e153361f87b2969","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Title vs Context / Problem","norm_id":"nd07889e9295aeec4","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An executor measuring `len(gc.get_objects())` against the title's '100k objects' gets a different number and doubts the fix."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Retitle: 'Each MCP gate run leaves ~115k allocated blocks (botocore service-model data) alive after it finishes'.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8571,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Make the regression test's loop teardown mirror the production gate-thread lifecycle (or drive it through the same helper the `*_start` thread uses), and state in the plan what that lifecycle is.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.net-mechanism","project.portability"],"criteria":["E5"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"ensure_current_event_loop() drives a coroutine that awaits anyio.to_thread.run_sync, then closes and unsets the loop\"","Context: the leak was measured with \"each on its own daemon thread (the MCP `*_start` shape)\"; the plan does not state what that thread does with its loop on exit"],"finding":"The regression test may not reproduce the production teardown that leaked. The test 'closes and unsets the loop' explicitly before checking the weakref. The plan never says whether rebar's per-gate-thread path (`ensure_current_event_loop` on an MCP `*_start` daemon thread) closes and unsets its loop the same way. If the fix's effectiveness depends on that teardown, the test stays green while the real gate-thread path is not covered.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f50ca0b486c4f411f","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing — first bullet ('then closes and unsets the loop')","norm_id":"n2bc12ed76520bab6","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Gate threads in production exit without closing their loop. The test, which does close it, passes. A future anyio or rebar change re-introduces retention that only an unclosed or still-set loop exposes, and no test catches it."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Make the regression test follow the production lifecycle: on a short-lived thread, call `ensure_current_event_loop()`, drive the coroutine on that loop without closing or unsetting it, join the thread, then `gc.collect()` and assert the loop weakref is dead (for both the successful and the raising drive).","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.6,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'drives a coroutine that awaits anyio.to_thread.run_sync, then closes and unsets the loop'","src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py:534-536 — `loop = asyncio.new_event_loop(); asyncio.set_event_loop(loop); return loop` with no matching close/unset","search for `set_event_loop(None)` in src/rebar finds only the docstring at model_classes.py:515; callers in runner.py:567 and structured_run.py:217/256 never close the loop"],"finding":"The regression test closes and unsets the loop before checking that it was collected. Production never does this: `ensure_current_event_loop` installs a loop and leaves it installed, and no code in src/ closes it or calls `set_event_loop(None)`. In the real gate path the loop is released only when the gate thread exits and asyncio's per-thread loop storage is dropped. So the test proves collectability under a teardown production doesn't perform, not the MCP `*_start` daemon-thread lifecycle the leak was measured on.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1dec35ff11e3bee0","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing — 'then closes and unsets the loop; after gc.collect() a weakref to that loop must be dead'","norm_id":"n197542f443c013f0","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future anyio or asyncio change keeps a never-closed loop alive after its thread exits. The test still passes because it closes the loop explicitly, while the gate path leaks again.","A later rebar change keeps a gate thread's loop alive past the run. Production regresses but the test stays green."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In tests/unit/test_model_classes.py, inside the worker thread, take the loop from `ensure_current_event_loop()`, record `weakref.ref(loop)`, and call `loop.run_until_complete(coro())`, where `coro` awaits `anyio.to_thread.run_sync(...)` and in the failure variant raises after it. Don't close or unset the loop. Join the thread, delete local references, run `gc.collect()`, and assert `ref() is None`. If ResourceWarning noise from the unclosed loop matters, filter it inside the test.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.6111,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"insufficient","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a proving command for the RED half (e.g. `uv run --with anyio==4.14.2 pytest tests/unit/test_model_classes.py -k <test>` must fail) and record its output on the ticket.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["E6","F1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.5214,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Testing: 'Verified in scratch: fails on anyio 4.14.2 (loop retained), passes on 4.15.0.'","No command or recorded output is specified for the 4.14.2 run."],"finding":"The AC requires a test that 'fails on anyio 4.14.2 and passes on the locked version', but no step or command shows the RED half. Once uv.lock moves to 4.15.0, normal CI and `make verify` only ever run the GREEN half, so the fail-on-4.14.2 claim has no in-session proving command.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fba8b6e5d1202d607","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria: 'tests/unit/test_model_classes.py contains a test that fails on anyio 4.14.2 and passes on the locked version'","norm_id":"na07fb475fba4e339","priority":0.0786,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reviewer cannot tell whether the committed test (as opposed to the scratch version) really detects the leak.","A later refactor of the test silently stops exercising the root-task RunVar, and nothing shows it."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Under Testing, add: 'RED proof: `uv run --with anyio==4.14.2 pytest tests/unit/test_model_classes.py -k loop_collectable` fails for both the success and raising variants; output pasted as a ticket comment. GREEN: the same command under the lock passes.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1429,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Correct the portability bullet to list anyio, and state that the test is guarded with `pytest.importorskip(\"anyio\")` (or that the unit leg always installs the extras).","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["COH","E2"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.6,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'drives a coroutine that awaits `anyio.to_thread.run_sync`'","Approach: floor declared 'in the `agents` and `mcp` extras'"],"finding":"The Testing section claims the test 'uses only threads, asyncio and weakref', but it awaits `anyio.to_thread.run_sync` and calls rebar's `ensure_current_event_loop()`. anyio comes in through the `agents`/`mcp` extras, and the plan does not say whether the test skips when those extras are absent, e.g. in a core-only or lowest-direct leg.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4a20cd519a8de808","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing: 'Portability: the test uses only threads, asyncio and weakref'","norm_id":"n9cddd468913e50e6","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A unit-test leg installed without the agents/mcp extras fails with ImportError on anyio instead of skipping."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Portability: 'uses threads, asyncio, weakref and anyio (skipped via `pytest.importorskip(\"anyio\")` when the agents/mcp extras are not installed); no POSIX-only API.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.3125,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"insufficient","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify that the test joins the driving thread and waits for anyio worker-thread shutdown (or polls gc and the weakref with a bounded deadline) before asserting the loop is dead.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.net-mechanism","project.portability"],"criteria":["E5"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"after `gc.collect()` a weakref to that loop must be dead\"","No statement that the driving thread is joined, or that anyio worker threads are drained, before the collect/assert"],"finding":"The weakref-dead assertion may be timing-sensitive. `anyio.to_thread.run_sync` runs work on anyio worker threads, which are stopped by a callback on the root task. The plan checks the weakref right after `gc.collect()` but does not say the test waits for those worker threads (or the gate thread) to fully exit first. A thread still winding down could hold a transient reference to the loop.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f64f328b8aabb5802","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing — first and second bullets ('after gc.collect() a weakref to that loop must be dead')","norm_id":"n7434bee8d6f480c7","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["On a loaded CI runner the worker thread has not finished exiting when `gc.collect()` runs, so the weakref is still alive and `make verify` fails intermittently on the fixed anyio version."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.125,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"insufficient","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"insufficient","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Record on the ticket the exact measurement script/command and the ≥10-run 4.15.0 numbers, plus the command and output showing the new test failing under anyio 4.14.2 (e.g. `uv run --with anyio==4.14.2 pytest ...`).","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.net-mechanism","project.portability"],"criteria":["E3","E5"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8714,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC: \"measured over at least 10 gate runs in one process ... recorded as a comment\"","Root cause: \"anyio 4.15.0 -> flat (543,052 -> 544,109 blocks over 4 runs, 7 OrderedDicts)\"","AC: \"a test that fails on anyio 4.14.2 and passes on the locked version\""],"finding":"Two acceptance criteria rest on one-off scratch evidence that the repo will not reproduce. The test 'fails on anyio 4.14.2' cannot be re-checked once uv.lock moves to 4.15.0. The ≥10-run flat-blocks measurement uses a scratch harness the plan does not commit or describe. The 4.15.0 evidence given so far covers only 4 runs, below the AC's own 10-run threshold.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f59094766890a3577","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria — items 2 and 4; Root cause — 'anyio